tion":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.0171669,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.00896296,"nucleus_score":-2.4568,"pct_ad":0.256222,"pct_control":0.26275,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.896005,"donor_log2fc":0.0184686,"donor_lfcse":0.0375344,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00458048,"degas_log2fc":-0.0570833,"degas_padj":9.9881e-05},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"AXIN2","gene_symbol_current":"AXIN2","gene_id":"ENSG00000168646","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":-0.0206452,"donor_lfcse":0.117294,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-1.55853e-06,"degas_log2fc":-0.125345,"degas_padj":0.211446},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"AXIN2","gene_symbol_current":"AXIN2","gene_id":"ENSG00000168646","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.993481,"donor_log2fc":-0.00803265,"donor_lfcse":0.132344,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.000481119,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000168646","entrez_id":["8313"],"uniprot":["Q9Y2T1"],"ncbi_summary":"The Axin-related protein, Axin2, presumably plays an important role in the regulation of the stability of beta-catenin in the Wnt signaling pathway, like its rodent homologs, mouse conductin/rat axil. In mouse, conductin organizes a multiprotein complex of APC (adenomatous polyposis of the colon), beta-catenin, glycogen synthase kinase 3-beta, and conductin, which leads to the degradation of beta-catenin. Apparently, the deregulation of beta-catenin is an important event in the genesis of a number of malignancies. The AXIN2 gene has been mapped to 17q23-q24, a region that shows frequent loss of heterozygosity in breast cancer, neuroblastoma, and other tumors. Mutations in this gene have been associated with colorectal cancer with defective mismatch repair. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9Y2T1","text":"Inhibitor of the Wnt signaling pathway. Down-regulates beta-catenin. Probably facilitate the phosphorylation of beta-catenin and APC by GSK3B."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}